/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.

    Written to attack the store rules (2026-11-17 review): maker keeps its argument. A rabbit's series reaches
    something that outlives the rabbit (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Define object bag with (the series of series of number items).
Bind making a bag to bag-around, given (the series of series of number rows):
    Return a new bag { the items rows }.
Done.
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define b as cast bag-around on (keeper).
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Insert inner into b's items.
Done.

Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State keeper.
